<title>UK: North Sea June crude liftings seen down 260,000 bp.</title>
<headline>North Sea June crude liftings seen down 260,000 bp.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>June loading schedules for the eight main British and Norwegian oilfield systems project liftings will fall by about 260,000 barrels per day (bpd) from May, programmes released this week by operating companies show.</p>
<p>Daily liftings in June from Norway's Ekofisk, Gullfaks, Oseberg, Statfjord and Troll and Britain's Brent, Flotta and Forties systems are scheduled at 4.35 million bpd, down from 4.61 million bpd in May, the programmes show.</p>
<p>June programmes project 212 cargoes versus 234 in the longer month of May.</p>
<p>The thinner loading schedules are mainly the result of heavy maintenance programmes, particularly at the Forties and Oseberg systems.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
